{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"waterish-aquamarine-bug","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter the code stories of epic nonblack-brigandish-guillemot land, user docs and runbooks still describe the repo-pinned trust file `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `rebar trusted-env`, pinned-key trust bases and log-position key eras. The files that name it on main today are `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/mcp-auth.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md` and `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` (from `git grep -l trusted_environments`). `AGENTS.md` (\"Certified ops\" paragraph) describes the enforcement flip as setting `verify.require_environment` + `verify.opcert_enforce_since` only. Sequencing: built on the removal story's merged commit.\n\n## Approach\nRewrite each passage to ADR 0125's model: validity-only by default (signature valid under its embedded key, subject bound, result reports `signing_key` and environment); optional `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` in the verifying environment's own config with the `untrusted` verdict; `verify.require_environment` requires a trust list; signing is never gated. Replace instructions that edit the pin file or run `rebar trusted-env` with the trust-list equivalent (env var `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS` in a deployment, or the user config `~/.config/rebar/config.toml`). In `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`, the preconditions name the MCP deployment's trust list (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` and `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`) instead of the pin file, the flip sets `require_environment`, `opcert_enforce_since` and a `trusted_opcert_keys` list in the gating environment's config (CI or the verifying clone), and rollback unsets them. Update the AGENTS.md sentence to name the trust list as part of the flip. Add a `docs/release-notes.md` entry: `rebar trusted-env` and `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` removed; new `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`; new verdict `untrusted`; `trust_basis` values now `envelope_key` and `trust_list`; new `signing_key` field. Historical ADRs (0049, 0098, 0100, 0104) are records and keep their text.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/mcp-auth.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`\n- `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`, `AGENTS.md`\nOut of scope: code, ADRs, eval corpora and test fixtures that quote the old filename as data.\n\n## Testing\nDocumentation-only; no new testable behavior. Docs drift and link tests run under `make verify`. Portability: Markdown only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'trusted_environments|trusted-env' -- docs infra AGENTS.md ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/release-notes.md'` prints no hits (release notes may name the removed items).\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` describes the flip and rollback with `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` and names the MCP deployment's list in compose and autodeploy (checked by reading the merged file).\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` records the removal, the new key, the `untrusted` verdict, the `trust_basis` change and `signing_key`.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","id":"70d0-4528-d074-40d3","parent_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Docs and runbooks describe per-environment op-cert trust lists instead of the repo pin file"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795112648896220579,"uuid":"54951943-9f06-4f4c-b043-ee218c58b822"}